Coding problems:
	Arithemtic:
		Sum and Difference – Given two integers, find their sum and difference.
		Product and Quotient – Given two integers, compute their product and quotient (integer division).
		Modulo Operations – Compute the remainder when one number is divided by another.
		Power Calculation – Given two numbers, compute using pow() or a loop.
		LCM and GCD – Given two numbers, find their Least Common Multiple (LCM) and Greatest Common Divisor (GCD).
		Sum of Digits – Given an integer, find the sum of its digits.
		Reversing a Number – Reverse the digits of a given number without using strings.
		Factorial Calculation – Compute the factorial of a given number using recursion or loops.
		Check for Prime – Determine if a given number is prime or not.
		Average of Two Numbers – Find the average of two integers (handle floating-point precision).
		Nth Fibonacci Number – Compute the Nth Fibonacci number using recursion or an optimized approach.
		Number of Divisors – Count the number of divisors of a given integer.
		Sum of First N Natural Numbers – Compute the sum of the first N natural numbers using formulas.
		Perfect Number Check – Check if a number is a perfect number (sum of its divisors equals the number).
	15	Armstrong Number – Check if a number is an Armstrong number (sum of cubes of its digits equals the number).
	
	Conditional loops:
		Even or Odd – Given an integer, check if it is even or odd.
		Maximum of Three Numbers – Find the largest of three numbers using if-else.
		Grade Calculation – Given a student's marks, assign a grade (A/B/C/D/F).
		Leap Year Checker – Check if a given year is a leap year or not.
		Calculator Program – Implement a simple calculator using a switch-case statement.
		Sum of N Natural Numbers – Compute the sum of the first N natural numbers.
		Reverse a Number – Reverse the digits of a given number.
		Factorial Calculation – Compute the factorial of a number using a loop.
		Multiplication Table – Print the multiplication table of a given number.
		Number of Digits in an Integer – Count the number of digits in a given integer.
		Check for Prime Number – Determine if a number is prime or not.
		Armstrong Number – Check if a number is an Armstrong number (sum of cubes of digits = number).
		Fibonacci Series – Print the first N Fibonacci numbers using a loop.
		Sum of Digits – Compute the sum of all digits of a given number.
	30	Perfect Number Check – Check if a number is a perfect number (sum of divisors = number).
		
		
	Bitwise:
		Bitwise AND, OR, XOR – Given two integers, compute their AND, OR, and XOR values.
		Check if a Number is Even or Odd using Bitwise – Use the bitwise AND (&) operator to check if a number is even or odd.
		Swap Two Numbers Without Using a Third Variable – Swap two numbers using the XOR operator.
		Multiply a Number by 2 Without Using * Operator – Multiply a number by 2 using the left shift (<<) operator.
		Divide a Number by 2 Without Using / Operator – Divide a number by 2 using the right shift (>>) operator.
		Check if a Number is a Power of Two – Use bitwise operations to check if a number is a power of 2.
		Count the Number of Set Bits (Hamming Weight) – Count the number of 1s in a binary representation of a number.
		Find the Only Non-Repeating Element in an Array – Given an array where every number appears twice except one, find the unique element using XOR.
		Turn Off the Rightmost Set Bit – Given a number, turn off its rightmost 1-bit (change it to 0).
		Check if Two Numbers Differ by Only One Bit – Given two numbers, check if they differ by exactly one bit.
		Find XOR of All Numbers from 1 to N – Compute XOR of all numbers from 1 to N efficiently.
		Find the Position of the Rightmost Set Bit – Find the position (1-based) of the rightmost 1-bit in a number.
		Toggle a Specific Bit of a Number – Toggle the K-th bit of a number (flip from 0 to 1 or 1 to 0).
		Find Two Non-Repeating Elements in an Array – Given an array where every element appears twice except two, find those two unique numbers using XOR.
	45	Binary Representation of a Number – Print the binary representation of a given number without using built-in functions.
		
	Arrays:
		Find the Maximum and Minimum Element in an Array – Given an array, find the largest and smallest elements.
		Reverse an Array – Reverse the elements of an array without using extra space.
		Sum of All Elements in an Array – Compute the sum of all elements in an array.
		Find the Second Largest Element in an Array – Find the second-largest number in an array.
		Count Occurrences of an Element in an Array – Given an array and a number, count its occurrences.
		Check if an Array is Sorted – Determine whether an array is sorted in non-decreasing order.
		Left Rotate an Array by One Position – Shift all elements left by one position.
		Right Rotate an Array by K Positions – Rotate an array to the right by K positions.
		Move All Zeros to the End – Given an array, move all zeroes to the end while maintaining order.
		Find the Union and Intersection of Two Arrays – Compute the union and intersection of two arrays.
		Find the Missing Number in an Array – Given an array of size N-1 with numbers from 1 to N, find the missing number.
		Find the First Repeating Element – Find the first element that appears more than once.
		Find the Subarray with Given Sum – Given an array and a target sum, find a subarray with that sum.
		Kadane’s Algorithm (Maximum Subarray Sum) – Find the maximum sum of a contiguous subarray.
	60	Find the Leader Elements in an Array – An element is a leader if it is greater than all elements to its right.
		
	strings:
		Reverse a String – Reverse a given string without using built-in functions.
		Check if a String is Palindrome – Determine if a given string reads the same forward and backward.
		Convert a String to Uppercase and Lowercase – Implement functions to convert a string to uppercase and lowercase.
		Count Vowels and Consonants in a String – Given a string, count the number of vowels and consonants.
		Find the Length of a String Without Using strlen() – Implement a function to compute the length of a string.
		Check if Two Strings are Anagrams – Determine if two strings contain the same characters in a different order.
		Find the First Non-Repeating Character – Identify the first unique character in a string.
		Remove All Spaces from a String – Remove all whitespace characters from a given string.
		Count the Number of Words in a String – Given a sentence, count the total number of words.
		Check if a String Contains Only Digits – Verify if a given string consists of only numeric characters.
		Find the Longest Common Prefix Among Strings – Given an array of strings, find the longest common prefix.
		Find All Substrings of a String – Generate and print all possible substrings of a given string.
		Implement strstr() Function – Write a function to find the first occurrence of one string within another.
		Find the Most Frequent Character in a String – Determine the character that appears most frequently.
	75	Check if a String is a Rotation of Another – Determine if one string is a rotated version of another (e.g., "abcde" and "cdeab").

	vectors:
		Insert and Print Elements in a Vector – Read N integers and store them in a vector. Print all elements.
		Reverse a Vector – Given a vector, reverse its elements.
		Find Maximum and Minimum in a Vector – Find the largest and smallest elements in a vector.
		Sort a Vector – Sort the elements of a vector in ascending and descending order.
		Remove Duplicates from a Vector – Remove all duplicate elements and print the unique elements.
		Find the Frequency of Each Element in a Vector – Count occurrences of each unique element.
		Rotate a Vector to the Left by K Positions – Perform a left rotation on a vector by K positions.
		Find the Sum of All Elements in a Vector – Compute the sum of all elements.
		Find the Second Largest Element in a Vector – Find the second-largest number in a vector.
		Find the Intersection of Two Vectors – Given two vectors, find the common elements between them.
		Check if a Vector is Sorted – Determine whether a vector is sorted in non-decreasing order.
		Find the First Repeating Element in a Vector – Identify the first element that appears more than once.
		Implement Binary Search on a Sorted Vector – Search for an element in a sorted vector using binary search.
		Merge Two Sorted Vectors – Merge two sorted vectors into one sorted vector.
	90	Find the Longest Consecutive Sequence in a Vector – Given an unsorted vector, find the longest sequence of consecutive numbers.

	oops:
		Create a Class and Object – Define a Student class with attributes name, age, and marks, and create an object to display its values.
		Constructor and Destructor – Implement a Car class with a constructor to initialize brand and model and a destructor to print a message when the object is destroyed.
		Encapsulation – Implement a BankAccount class with private attributes for account balance and public methods for deposit and withdrawal.
		Getter and Setter Methods – Create a Rectangle class with private attributes length and width, and provide getter and setter methods.
		Static Members – Implement a Counter class where every object shares a static variable that keeps track of the number of objects created.
		Operator Overloading – Overload the + operator for a ComplexNumber class to add two complex numbers.
		Function Overloading – Implement function overloading in a MathOperations class to calculate the sum of two or three numbers.
		Inheritance (Single Inheritance) – Create a Person base class and a Student derived class with an extra attribute rollNumber.
		Multiple Inheritance – Implement a HybridCar class inheriting from ElectricCar and PetrolCar.
		Hierarchical Inheritance – Create a base class Animal and derive Dog and Cat classes from it.
		Abstract Class and Pure Virtual Function – Implement an abstract class Shape with a pure virtual function area(), then derive Circle and Rectangle classes.
		Function Overriding (Polymorphism) – Implement function overriding in a base class Employee and a derived class Manager to display different salary calculations.
		Friend Function – Use a friend function to allow access to private members of two different classes.
		File Handling in OOP – Create a FileHandler class with methods to write and read data from a file.
	105	Template Class – Implement a generic class Box<T> that can store any data type using templates.

